==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gmw-pro|gem-pro}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|weize}}, {{m|gmh|weizze}}, {{m|gmh|weitze}}, from {{inh|de|goh|weizi}}, {{m|goh|weizzi}}.

The originally predominant High German form was {{m|de|Weiße|Weiße(n)}} (perhaps still in {{m|de|Weißbier}}; see there). The form with {{IPAchar|[ts]}} was a chiefly southern variant, which was standardised probably to avoid the homophony with the adjective {{m|de|weiß}}. Cognate with {{cog|lb|Weess}}, {{cog|hrx|Weize}}, {{cog|nl|weit}}, {{cog|nds|Weten}}, {{cog|fy|weet}}, {{cog|en|wheat}}.

